// Filename:	TS056 CL Auto 2 Array PCB.test
// Project:		CL Auto 2
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    14/08/25
//
// Description: test ing the LED array PCB-draft
// [ <addr_byte>  0x08  <reg>  <data> ]
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

{0} force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Equipment Setup 1
a. Connect the 3v3 pull up and connect the GND to the Bus Priate cable.
b. Connect the Arry1 lead to + of channel 1 on the PSU.
c. Connect the Arry2 lead to + of channel 2 on the PSU.
d. Connect the VPWR lead to + of channel 3 on the PSU.
e. Connect the GND's of channel 1, 2 & 3 together.
e. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #1: 

#2: Equipment Setup 2 & Configure the PSU
a. Connect the LED Array PCB to the TEXX (Refer to setup picture below).
b. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:1.010
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET2:1.010
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:16.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:16.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:1.000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1
CLICK_OK:


#3: Connect and Configure the Bus Pirate
CONNECT: BUS_PIRATE
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE m4
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 3
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE W
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE P
//EXE: OpenWinCam.bat

#4:Configure IC11 for temp and read AIN4 TH3 MSB & LSB for temperature:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x22 0x08 0x05 0x00}  
SUB: READ_SENSOR
//checks . . . MSB = %RS_MSB%, LSB = %RS_LSB% and decimal result = %RESULT%
-------------------------------------
Voltage = [3.3 * %RESULT% / (16 * 4095)]V
-------------------------------------
SET: Voltage = [3.3 * %RESULT% / (16 * 4095)]
-------------------------------------
RANGE: %Voltage% 2.55 0.15 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#5:Configure IC11 for temp and read AIN5 TH1 MSB & LSB for temperature:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x22 0x08 0x05 0x00}   
SUB: READ_SENSOR_2
//Checks . . . MSB = %RS_MSB%, LSB = %RS_LSB% and decimal result = %RESULT%
-------------------------------------
Voltage = [3.3 * %RESULT% / (16 * 4095)]V
-------------------------------------
SET: Voltage = [3.3 * %RESULT% / (16 * 4095)]
-------------------------------------
RANGE: %Voltage% 2.55 0.15 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#5:Configure IC11 for temp and read AIN6 TH2 MSB & LSB for temperature:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x22 0x08 0x05 0x00}   
SUB: READ_SENSOR_3
//Checks . . . MSB = %RS_MSB%, LSB = %RS_LSB% and decimal result = %RESULT%
-------------------------------------
Voltage = [3.3 * %RESULT% / (16 * 4095)]V
-------------------------------------
SET: Voltage = [3.3 * %RESULT% / (16 * 4095)]
-------------------------------------
RANGE: %Voltage% 2.55 0.15 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#6:  Configure IC9 & IC10 for test:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x40 0x0A 0x80} {0x40 0x00 0x00} {0x40 0x0A 0xFF} 
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x24 0x08 0x05 0xFC} //DELAY: 100 
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x24 0x08 0x07 0xFC} //(0x07)GPIO direction ,CH7..2=Output, CH1..0=Input//DELAY: 100
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x24 0x08 0x09 0xFC} //(0x09) Output driver type CH7..2=Push-pull//DELAY: 100
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x24 0x08 0x0B 0xFC}//(0x0B)Output levels CH7..2=High, CH1..0=Low
//CLICK_OK:

#7: Configure IC11 (Blue_Violet_Config)for LED test:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x22 0x08 0x05 0x04} //(0x07)GPIO direction ,CH7..2=Output, CH1..0=Input
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x22 0x08 0x07 0x04} //(0x09) Output driver type CH7..2=Push-pull
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x22 0x08 0x09 0x04} //(0x0B)Output levels CH7..2=High, CH1..0=Low
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x22 0x08 0x0B 0x04} //
//CLICK_OK:

#8:ALL LEDs OFF driver 1
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x40 0x0A 0xFF} // Turn OFF LEDS
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x24 0x08 0x0B 0xFC} // Turn OFF LEDS
DELAY: 100 
//CLICK_OK:

#9: AmberAD2.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x40 0x0A 0xBF} // LED ON
DELAY: 4000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 1.000 0.005 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

